! mcp_bootstrap_p105.strap -- printed page 105, the SECOND HALF of
! the MCP PSEUDO-OPERATION CODE TABLE that printed p.104 begins.
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.112, header READ AND NOT ASSUMED:
! the top line prints "TIME CLOCK 00054041  PUNID 11D11MCP  CARD ID
! CB000050  DIST. OF 3/01   3/01   PAGE NUMBER 105", and the page
! number was rendered on its own at 600 dpi and reads 105.  The TIME
! CLOCK is the same 00054041 that every page since printed p.97
! prints; the PUNID is p.99's 11D11MCP; the card-ID prefix is the
! "CB" p.104 carries.
!
! FIFTY-SIX LINES, AND THAT IS COUNTED, NOT ESTIMATED.  The printed
! line numbers run 1 to 56 with no gap and the rightmost column
! prints one card serial per line, CB000050 through CB000105 --
! 105-50+1 = 56, so the two counts agree and nothing fell off the
! top or the bottom of the render.  Below line 56 the page is blank.
!
! >>> THE WHOLE PAGE IS DEFINITIONS AND NOT ONE CARD COMPILES A
! WORD. <<<  Seventeen SYN cards define seventeen symbols; the other
! thirty-nine cards are comment cards.  17 + 39 = 56.  So this
! deck's entire check surface is SEVENTEEN SYMBOLS AND ZERO LISTING
! ROWS -- printed p.99's convention, which p.104 also follows: a SYN
! deposits no storage word, so it is checked in !SYM and must NOT be
! faked into a !CHECK.  There are no !CHECK lines below and that is
! correct.  The BINARY OUTPUT column prints "+00000000" and the data
! description "NULL" on all seventeen, which is the column working
! correctly on a definitions page, not a crop in the wrong place.
!
! THE SEVENTEEN, in printed order:
!   line  1  S FREE  12.32   000014.40+     line 24  DSIT    36.0   000044.00+
!   line  2  DIODEF  13.0    000015.00+     line 31  D DUMP  64.0   000100.00+
!   line 15  D SIO   32.0    000040.00+     line 33  D EOJ   65.0   000101.00+
!   line 16  D RIO   32.32   000040.40+     line 34  D HOLD  65.32  000101.40+
!   line 17  D RET   33.0    000041.00+     line 35  DRESLD  66.0   000102.00+
!   line 18  S D RET SYN,D RET 000041.00+   line 36  D FETCH 66.32  000102.40+
!   line 22  D TIME  35.0    000043.00+     line 38  D SPR   67.32  000103.40+
!   line 23  D COMM  35.32   000043.40+     line 39  D ABEOJ 68.0   000104.00+
!                                           line 40  D SCR   68.32  000104.40+
!
! FIRST printed location 000014.40+ (line 1), LAST 000104.40+ (line
! 40).  ALL SEVENTEEN CARRY THE TRAILING "+".  These are SYN VALUES,
! NOT ASSEMBLY ADDRESSES: the location counter does not advance by
! one bit anywhere on this page, so THERE IS NO ADDRESS CHAIN TO
! CLOSE ACROSS IT and none should be attempted.  printed pp.99-104
! are the same kind of page.
!
! >>> THE CHECK THE PAGE PERFORMS ON ITSELF, AND IT IS 17 OF 17.
! <<<  Each SYN prints its word.bit offset in DECIMAL in the
! STATEMENT column and the same offset in OCTAL in the LOCATION
! column, and every one of the seventeen agrees: 12.32/000014.40,
! 13.0/000015.00, 32.0/000040.00, 32.32/000040.40, 33.0/000041.00,
! 35.0/000043.00, 35.32/000043.40, 36.0/000044.00, 64.0/000100.00,
! 65.0/000101.00, 65.32/000101.40, 66.0/000102.00, 66.32/000102.40,
! 67.32/000103.40, 68.0/000104.00, 68.32/000104.40, and line 18's
! symbolic SYN,D RET resolves to line 17's 000041.00.  That is a
! real check of the digits, though not of the card.
!
! >>> THERE IS NO SLC ON THIS PAGE AND THIS DECK WRITES NONE. <<<
! p.104 line 6 printed "SLC,$" at 215020.71; p.105 prints no SLC row
! at all and emits no storage, so the counter leaves this page
! exactly where it arrived, still 215020.71.  Every value below is
! an absolute literal, so the deck assembles standalone with no
! origin and the verifier passes 17 of 17 without one.  Writing an
! SLC here would record a fact the page does not state.
!   >>> AND IT ANSWERS p.104's OPEN QUESTION, IN THE NEGATIVE. <<<
!   p.104's header asks whether p.105 resumes at 215020.71 and notes
!   that this is "testable only at p.105's first card that EMITS
!   STORAGE, if it has one".  IT HAS NONE.  So the p.103/p.104/p.105
!   counter join is still untested and rolls forward to the first
!   page after this one that spends a bit.
!
! >>> NO EXTERNAL SYMBOL IS REFERENCED ANYWHERE ON THIS PAGE. <<<
! Sixteen of the seventeen cards carry a literal word.bit offset
! written on the card itself, and the seventeenth -- line 18's
! "S D RET SYN,D RET" -- names D RET, which line 17 defines one row
! above it.  There are no SYN stand-ins to declare and none appear
! below.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT THE PAGE CONTAINS, IN FOUR BLOCKS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Lines 1-14   the tail of the I/O pseudo-ops p.104 starts: $FREE at
!              12.32 and $IODEF at 13.0 compile; the twelve tape-mode
!              codes 14.0-16.33 (HD/LD density, EVEN/ODD parity,
!              ECC/NOECC) are all COMMENTED OUT.
! Lines 15-27  the service pseudo-ops 32.0-37.32.  Nine compile, six
!              are commented out.
! Lines 28-40  a box heading, "******** PSEUDO-OPS WITH TENTACLES
!              ********" (line 29), and the major-package codes
!              64.0-68.32.  Nine compile, D EDUMP (64.32) and D SPU
!              (67.0) are commented out.
! Lines 41-56  two more box headings, "******** RESERVED FOR FUTURE
!              MCP USE ********" (line 42) and "******** RESERVED FOR
!              INSTALLATION PSEUDO OPS ********" (line 55), and ten
!              unnamed reserved slots 69.0-73.32 (lines 44-53), all
!              comment cards.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE NAMES ARE CORROBORATED BY TWO PRIMARY SOURCES, AND BE PRECISE
! ABOUT HOW THEY WERE READ
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> BOTH WERE READ IN docs/ocr/, NOT RENDERED OFF THE PDF. <<<
! They are modern typeset manuals rather than this drum, so their
! OCR is far cleaner than the listing's, but they are still the
! weaker evidence class that printed p.103's deck labelled for
! SDISIC/SPRIME/SPRIMR/SIT.  Said out loud rather than smoothed.
!
! (a) docs/C22-6728_7030_MCP_Sys_Analysis_Guide.pdf, FIGURE 13 "The
!     Service Pseudo-Ops" and FIGURE 14 "Major Package Pseudo-Ops"
!     (docs/ocr/C22-6728_7030_MCP_Sys_Analysis_Guide.txt:4085-4125).
!     Figure 13's third column runs
!       $CHEX 12.00  $FREE 12.32  $IODEF 13.00  $SIO 32.00
!       $RIO 32.32   $RET 33.00   $RAM 33.32    $STRG 34.00
!       $FECRG 34.32 $TIME 35.00  $COMM 35.32   $SIT 36.00
!     and Figure 14's left column runs
!       $DUMP 64.00  $EDUMP 64.32 $EOJ 65.00    $HOLD 65.32
!       $RESLD 66.00 $FETCH 66.32 $SPU 67.00    $SPR 67.32
!       $ABEOJ 68.00 $SCR 68.32
!     -- the same names at the same codes as this page's NAME and
!     STATEMENT columns, position for position, with the "$" where
!     this page writes "D ".  Figure 14's title is this page's own
!     line 29: "PSEUDO-OPS WITH TENTACLES".
!
! (b) docs/C22-6678-1_7030_MCP_Reference_Jun64.pdf, APPENDIX A, "MCP
!     PSEUDO-OPERATION CODES" (docs/ocr/..._Jun64.txt:5204-5244),
!     which adds the commented-out cards:
!       $HD 14.0  $HDS 14.01  $LD 14.32  $LDS 14.33
!       $EVEN 15.0 $EVENS 15.01 $ODD 15.32 $ODDS 15.33
!       $ECC 16.0 $ECCS 16.01 $NOECC 16.32 $NOECCS 16.33
!       $FIXUP 36.32 $STLR 37.0 $FELR 37.32
!
! >>> WHAT (b) RESCUED: ECC, NOT EOC. <<<  Lines 11-14 print
! "-DECC", "-DECCS", "-DNOECC", "-DNOECCS", and the first reading of
! this page took the third glyph for a damaged O and wrote DEOC /
! DNOEOC -- "end of chain" beside EVEN/ODD and HD/LD is a plausible
! English word and the drum opens round glyphs constantly, so the
! hazard pushes exactly that way.  Appendix A prints $ECC / $NOECC.
! The C's are genuine.  Nothing in this deck depends on it (all four
! are comment cards) but the correction is recorded because the same
! reflex would have been wrong on a card that compiled.
! (b) likewise settles line 21's "D FECRG" -- $FECRG 34.32 -- which
! is not an English word and could not have been settled by shape.
!
! >>> WHERE THE MANUALS DO NOT LINE UP, RECORDED AND NOT SMOOTHED.
! <<<
!   * FIGURE 13 PRINTS "$FREE" TWICE, at 10.32 and at 12.32.  p.104
!     line 44 declares D FREE at 10.32 and THIS page's line 1
!     declares S FREE at 12.32, so the listing uses two different
!     names for the manual's two $FREE rows.  Whether the manual has
!     a genuine duplicate or the OCR doubled a row cannot be told
!     from OCR, and the PDF page was not rendered.
!   * $ATID 17.0 and $ABEX 38.0 are in Appendix A and have NO CARD
!     on this page, commented or otherwise.  The 1964 manuals are a
!     later revision than this March 1963 listing; the absence is
!     recorded rather than passed over.
!   * THE MANUALS DO NOT CONFIRM THE "S" ON LINE 1 OR LINE 18.  They
!     give the CODE (12.32, 33.0); the PREFIX LETTER is this page's
!     own ink and nothing else.  It is clean: at 1800 dpi line 1's
!     first glyph is an unmistakable S and line 18 reads "S D RET"
!     with the same S and a stemmed D two characters along.
!
! >>> AND THREE LANDED DECKS ALREADY AGREE, WHICH IS THE STRONGEST
! EVIDENCE ON THIS PAGE. <<<  D RET and D COMM are not new here:
!   decks/mcp_bootstrap_p35.strap lines 108-109 carry
!     "DRET  SYN, 33.0" and "DCOMM SYN, 35.32" -- the IDENTICAL
!     statements, transcribed off printed p.35 lines 45-46;
!   decks/mcp_bootstrap_p34.strap:69 carries "DRET  SYN, (8)41.0";
!   decks/mcp_bootstrap_p79.strap:100 carries "DCOMM SYN, (8)43.40".
! 0o41.0 and 0o43.40 are exactly this page's printed locations for
! lines 17 and 23.  Three transcribers, three pages, one address
! each -- this is the cross-deck agreement check_symbol_spellings.py
! exists to find, and here it passes rather than fires.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! SUBSTITUTIONS AND OMISSIONS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! (1) BLANKS INSIDE SYMBOL NAMES ARE DROPPED, as on every page since
!     p.2.  The NAME column prints "S FREE", "D SIO", "D RIO",
!     "D RET", "S D RET", "D TIME", "D COMM", "D DUMP", "D EOJ",
!     "D HOLD", "D FETCH", "D SPR", "D ABEOJ", "D SCR"; "DIODEF",
!     "DSIT" and "DRESLD" are printed closed up with no blank, which
!     is how a six- or four-character name fills the field, and they
!     are NOT comment cards -- each prints a LOCATION and a BINARY
!     OUTPUT in its own column.
! (2) THE THIRTY-NINE COMMENT CARDS ARE NOT TRANSCRIBED.  They are
!     identified by p.104's two tells: (i) LOCATION and BINARY
!     OUTPUT are BOTH empty, and (ii) the card prints as a RAW CARD
!     IMAGE and its fields do not line up -- lines 21 and 32 print
!     "D FECRGSYN,34.32" and "D EDUMPSYN,64.32" with NO GAP before
!     SYN, which no compiled row on this page does.
!     They are, with the code each would have defined:
!       line  3 D HD   14.0     line  4 D HDS   14.01
!       line  5 D LD   14.32    line  6 D LDS   14.33
!       line  7 D EVEN 15.0     line  8 D EVENS 15.01
!       line  9 D ODD  15.32    line 10 D ODDS  15.33
!       line 11 D ECC  16.0     line 12 D ECCS  16.01
!       line 13 DNOECC 16.32    line 14 DNOECCS 16.33
!       line 19 D RAM  33.32    line 20 DSTRG   34.0
!       line 21 D FECRG 34.32   line 25 DFIXUP  36.32
!       line 26 DSTLR  37.0     line 27 DFELR   37.32
!       line 32 D EDUMP 64.32   line 37 D SPU   67.0
!     plus lines 28, 30, 41, 43, 54 and 56, which carry a bare "-";
!     lines 29, 42 and 55, the three box headings quoted above; and
!     lines 44-53, the ten reserved slots described below.
!     NONE of them is faked into a !SYM: a commented card defines
!     nothing, so there is nothing to check.
! (3) NOTHING ELSE.  strap_asm refused no printed spelling and no
!     printed operand on this page, and no row was altered to make
!     the assembler agree.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE GLYPHS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THIS PAGE OPENS ROUND GLYPHS FREELY and proves it in its own
! column headings: "LOCATION" prints "LCCATICN" at 900 dpi on both
! the left and the right rule.  EVERY LOCATION HERE IS AN OCTAL
! FIELD, printed "0000NN.NN+", so a round glyph there is a 0 with
! certainty -- line 2 renders "000015.CC+", line 17 "000041.CC+",
! line 24 "000044.CC+", line 40 "CCC104.4C+".  All zeros.  The
! STATEMENT column's bit offsets are DECIMAL and many print their 0
! open ("SYN,13.C", "SYN,32.C", "SYN,64.C"); all are 0, confirmed by
! their own LOCATION fields.
!
! THE C/D PAIR WAS THE ONLY REAL WORK, and it was settled on the
! LEFT SIDE of the glyph at 1800 dpi, not on the bowl: D has a
! straight vertical left stem with squared corners, C and O are
! round with no stem.  Rows zoomed to 1800 dpi for this: line 1
! (S, not D), line 2 (D-I-O-D-E-F: stems on characters 1 and 4, a
! round open O at 3), line 18 ("S D RET"), lines 22-24 ("D TIME",
! "D COMM", "DSIT" -- 23's leading glyph has the stem and its
! second and third characters are the round C and the open O of
! COMM), lines 33-39 ("D EOJ", "D HOLD", "DRESLD", "D FETCH",
! "D SPR", "D ABEOJ") and line 40 ("D SCR", whose leading D stands
! directly beside the stemless C of SCR in the same word).
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! LISTING MARKS AND TWO OBSERVATIONS NOT EXPLAINED
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! EVERY ONE of the fifty-six line numbers carries an asterisk right
! after it ("1*", "56*").  That is the ordinary column, as on
! pp.99 and 104, and is not a mark.  No row carries the second
! asterisk after its LOCATION that p.104 line 6 carries.  No mark
! changes a compiled bit, and this page compiles none.
!
! (A) >>> THE PAGE-HEADER "LOCATION" FIELD IS FILLED IN HERE AND
!     BLANK ON pp.103 AND 104. <<<  The right-hand end of this
!     page's column-heading rule prints "LOCATION   000014" -- six
!     octal digits, rendered on its own at 900 dpi.  000014 is the
!     WORD part of line 1's 000014.40.  The same field on PDF pp.110
!     and 111 (printed 103 and 104) prints "LOCATION" with NOTHING
!     after it, checked at 900 dpi and again at 400 dpi across the
!     full width of the rule.  What decides whether the field is
!     filled is NOT established here.  It is recorded because, on
!     this page, it is a free second witness to the first location.
!
! (B) >>> LINES 44-53 PRINT "$SYN,69.0" WITH A BLANK NAME FIELD AND
!     NO DASH, AND THE "$" IS NOT EXPLAINED. <<<  Under the heading
!     "RESERVED FOR FUTURE MCP USE" the page prints ten rows
!     $SYN,69.0 / 69.32 / 70.0 / 70.32 / 71.0 / 71.32 / 72.0 /
!     72.32 / 73.0 / 73.32.  They are comment cards by p.104's
!     tells -- LOCATION and BINARY OUTPUT are BOTH empty on all ten,
!     confirmed at 900 dpi -- so they define nothing and nothing
!     from them goes in this deck.  Two details are recorded as
!     OBSERVATIONS ONLY: the one-character dash column that lines
!     41, 42, 43, 54, 55 and 56 fill is BLANK on all ten, and the
!     "$" prints exactly one character to the LEFT of where every
!     compiled row's "SYN" begins.  A plain reading is that these
!     are notes reserving ten codes for pseudo-ops not yet named,
!     with "$" standing in for the absent name, but that is a
!     reading and not a measurement and it is not relied on.
!     Corroboration that the slots were later filled, from the same
!     weaker OCR class as above: C22-6728 Figure 14's right column
!     gives SJC1 76.32, SOUTPT 77.0, SSPEOJ 77.32, SDDT 78.0,
!     SJC4 78.32, SSCR4 79.0, SKOM 79.32, SCOMD 80.0, SLOG4 80.32,
!     SLOG2 81.0, SLOG1 81.32 -- a different range, so the 1964
!     expansion did not use 69-73 either.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> THE CARD SERIAL SKIPS CB000049. <<<
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! printed p.104's deck counts its serials CB000001..CB000048,
! "counted, not estimated", and its last printed serial was
! re-rendered at 600 dpi for this page and is CB000048, with the
! paper blank below it.  This page's header card ID and its line 1
! both read CB000050, re-rendered at 900 dpi beside p.104's line 48
! in one montage.  CB000049 IS ON NEITHER PAGE.  Nothing in this
! deck depends on it -- no symbol, no bit, and the two pages' codes
! run 12.0 -> 12.32 -> 13.0 across the break with nothing missing
! from the manuals' sequence either -- but a card that was punched
! and not listed is worth knowing about, so it is recorded instead
! of rounded off.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> NO CROSS-DECK COLLISION. <<<
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Of the seventeen names, only D RET and D COMM appear in any other
! deck, and both AGREE (see above).  The other fifteen -- SFREE,
! DIODEF, DSIO, DRIO, SDRET, DTIME, DSIT, DDUMP, DEOJ, DHOLD,
! DRESLD, DFETCH, DSPR, DABEOJ, DSCR -- appear nowhere else in
! decks/.  In particular SFREE does NOT collide with p.104's DFREE:
! they are different names at different codes.  printed p.70 line 56
! is "T IPL3  B,DMCP" with the comment "-THEN UNLOAD WITH - SFREE -"
! and printed p.71 line 1's parameter half word is ",DFREE"
! compiling 000000.00 80, so the first assembly's DFREE is 0 there
! and the English name the comment uses for the operation is SFREE.
! That is a nice echo of this page's line 1 but it is NOT a check of
! it: the compiled parameter is DFREE, not SFREE.
!
! >>> AND THIS PAGE IS OUTSIDE THE TAIL SCOPE pp.2-98 SIT IN. <<<
! printed p.98 line 37's "UNTAIL,(2)" closed the TAIL,(2)G block
! that printed p.2 opened, and printed p.99 line 11's
! "SLC,(8)215000." moved the origin, so a name here that repeats a
! name from pp.2-98 is tail scope and not a collision.  Nothing on
! this page needed that excuse; it is noted for the next reader.

! ---- MCP PSEUDO-OPERATION CODES, the second half -------------------
! No SLC: see the header.  No externals: see the header.  The bit
! offsets are written DECIMAL exactly as the STATEMENT column prints
! them, and print OCTAL in the LOCATION column.
SFREE   SYN, 12.32                   ! line  1  S FREE
DIODEF  SYN, 13.0                    ! line  2  DIODEF
DSIO    SYN, 32.0                    ! line 15  D SIO
DRIO    SYN, 32.32                   ! line 16  D RIO
DRET    SYN, 33.0                    ! line 17  D RET  -- p.35 l.45 too
SDRET   SYN, DRET                    ! line 18  S D RET -- the page's
                                      !          only symbolic operand
DTIME   SYN, 35.0                    ! line 22  D TIME
DCOMM   SYN, 35.32                   ! line 23  D COMM -- p.35 l.46 too
DSIT    SYN, 36.0                    ! line 24  DSIT
DDUMP   SYN, 64.0                    ! line 31  D DUMP
DEOJ    SYN, 65.0                    ! line 33  D EOJ
DHOLD   SYN, 65.32                   ! line 34  D HOLD
DRESLD  SYN, 66.0                    ! line 35  DRESLD
DFETCH  SYN, 66.32                   ! line 36  D FETCH
DSPR    SYN, 67.32                   ! line 38  D SPR
DABEOJ  SYN, 68.0                    ! line 39  D ABEOJ
DSCR    SYN, 68.32                   ! line 40  D SCR

! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE PRINTED LISTING -- the seventeen cards that define a symbol.
! LOCATION, then BINARY OUTPUT with its data description, then NAME
! and STATEMENT.  All seventeen print "+00000000  NULL", which is
! what a SYN with no data description prints.
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
!   line  1  000014.40+  +00000000  NULL        S FREE   SYN,12.32
!   line  2  000015.00+  +00000000  NULL        DIODEF   SYN,13.0
!   line 15  000040.00+  +00000000  NULL        D SIO    SYN,32.0
!   line 16  000040.40+  +00000000  NULL        D RIO    SYN,32.32
!   line 17  000041.00+  +00000000  NULL        D RET    SYN,33.0
!   line 18  000041.00+  +00000000  NULL        S D RET  SYN,D RET
!   line 22  000043.00+  +00000000  NULL        D TIME   SYN,35.0
!   line 23  000043.40+  +00000000  NULL        D COMM   SYN,35.32
!   line 24  000044.00+  +00000000  NULL        DSIT     SYN,36.0
!   line 31  000100.00+  +00000000  NULL        D DUMP   SYN,64.0
!   line 33  000101.00+  +00000000  NULL        D EOJ    SYN,65.0
!   line 34  000101.40+  +00000000  NULL        D HOLD   SYN,65.32
!   line 35  000102.00+  +00000000  NULL        DRESLD   SYN,66.0
!   line 36  000102.40+  +00000000  NULL        D FETCH  SYN,66.32
!   line 38  000103.40+  +00000000  NULL        D SPR    SYN,67.32
!   line 39  000104.00+  +00000000  NULL        D ABEOJ  SYN,68.0
!   line 40  000104.40+  +00000000  NULL        D SCR    SYN,68.32

! ---- CHECKS, read by tests/verify_mcp_page.py 105 ----------------
! Seventeen symbols and NO rows: a SYN deposits no storage word, so
! there is nothing for a !CHECK to look at and none is written.
! The trailing "+" the page prints after every location is the SIGN,
! printed as a suffix the way printed p.84's negative SYN prints
! "000001.00-".  It is dropped here because listing_oracle.loc_bits
! parses a location as "word.bit" and has no sign field, and because
! every landed deck records the bare NNNNNN.NN -- p.99's convention.
!SYM   SFREE    000014.40
!SYM   DIODEF   000015.00
!SYM   DSIO     000040.00
!SYM   DRIO     000040.40
!SYM   DRET     000041.00
!SYM   SDRET    000041.00
!SYM   DTIME    000043.00
!SYM   DCOMM    000043.40
!SYM   DSIT     000044.00
!SYM   DDUMP    000100.00
!SYM   DEOJ     000101.00
!SYM   DHOLD    000101.40
!SYM   DRESLD   000102.00
!SYM   DFETCH   000102.40
!SYM   DSPR     000103.40
!SYM   DABEOJ   000104.00
!SYM   DSCR     000104.40
